          </h2>

          <p>
            Home air compressors fall into a few clear groups.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Pancake Compressors</h3>

          <p>
            Round 6-gallon tanks, like the CRAFTSMAN and Metabo HPT EC914S. Compact, affordable and the standard choice for nailers, but loud.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Quiet Compressors</h3>

          <p>
            The California Air Tools 8010A and Metabo HPT EC28M are listed at 60 and 59 decibels. They suit attached garages, basements and indoor trim work.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Oil-Lubricated and Wheeled Compressors</h3>

          <p>
            The Makita MAC2400 and Campbell Hausfeld VT6290 use cast-iron, oil-lubricated pumps that last longer and deliver more air, at the cost of weight and maintenance.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Portable Tire Inflators</h3>

          <p>
            The DEWALT DCC020IB is not a shop compressor. It is for tires, sports balls and air mattresses, with automatic shut-off.
          </p>

